  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Graveyard Keeper 2",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/22343/450x258/graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791349200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/22343-buy-graveyard-keeper-2-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-7cdec8e",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Very addicting, but late game is grindy and a lot of stuff isn't explained to you.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, the graveyard feels more like a second thought now. The game's story is more focused on helping rebuild the town and the new 'tower defender' mini game.\n\n\n\nThe game can be buggy at times. I have gotten myself softlocked by the most stupid things...Placing a building item too close to each other, walking too far at the docks (there is an invisible wall, that prevents you from going back lol), among other bugs that need to be fixed. If you play it on PC, you won't have much issues like our console fellows.\n\n\n\nThe zombie factory part should be fixed more and the devs have released plans on changing and fixing this, so I am hopeful.\n\n\n\nIf you liked the first one, I would still recommend GK2!"
    },
    {
      "game": "Crashout Crew",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/20607/450x258/crashout-crew-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791349200",
